       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum daily dose. The usual adult maximum is 2550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. Doses above that carry a high risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPlease confirm the intended regimen. Common options include:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **500 mg three times daily** (1500 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg once daily** (if an extended-release product was intended, though ER is usually capped at 2000 mg/day)\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, frequency, and formulation, I'll enter the order."
